# Code quality

- Follow repository naming, formatting and file-organization conventions.
- Prefer readable code over clever code.
- Keep functions and classes focused.
- Remove duplication only when the abstraction is stable and beneficial.
- Avoid speculative generalization.
- Avoid broad formatting-only diffs mixed with functional changes.
- Add comments for intent and non-obvious constraints, not for obvious syntax.
- Preserve error context.
- Do not swallow exceptions silently.
- Avoid dead code and unused imports introduced by the change.
